WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:01.980
Film Courage: When did the idea for Passionflix
begin?

00:00:01.980 --> 00:00:06.120
Passionflix Co-Founder and CEO, Tosca Musk:
The idea for Passionflix came about…it was

00:00:06.120 --> 00:00:07.560
actually Joany’s idea.

00:00:07.560 --> 00:00:10.530
Joany Kane is our founding partner.

00:00:10.530 --> 00:00:14.490
She had the idea quite a few years ago.

00:00:14.490 --> 00:00:19.450
When FIFTY SHADES OF GREY came out, she was
wondering why there isn’t a place for romance

00:00:19.450 --> 00:00:24.080
novels that had been turned into movies when
the movie was such a success.

00:00:24.080 --> 00:00:30.090
So she actually got the URL (passionflix.com)
and said “I’m going to do this.”

00:00:30.090 --> 00:00:32.739
And then many years later nothing happened
to it.

00:00:32.739 --> 00:00:38.210
Until one New Year’s Eve she decided ‘I’m
going to make it happen’ and she booked

00:00:38.210 --> 00:00:40.360
a flight to Los Angeles.

00:00:40.360 --> 00:00:44.920
And it just so happens that Joany and I had
met a few months prior.

00:00:44.920 --> 00:00:49.559
She had watched a movie of mine on Aeon [Network]
called YOU CAST A SPELL ON ME.

00:00:49.559 --> 00:00:53.070
And she contacted me the next day and said
“I absolutely loved your movie.

00:00:53.070 --> 00:00:58.489
I loved how you directed that movie and I
would really love it if you would take one

00:00:58.489 --> 00:01:01.449
of my movies and direct that.”

00:01:01.449 --> 00:01:06.420
And normally you get a lot of people that
solicit you and normally you’re like “No,

00:01:06.420 --> 00:01:07.920
I’m going to ignore that.”

00:01:07.920 --> 00:01:14.549
But her note was so sweet and she was just
so open in her communication to me that I

00:01:14.549 --> 00:01:16.200
was like “Okay, let me have a look at the
script.”

00:01:16.200 --> 00:01:17.819
And I was like “Oh!

00:01:17.819 --> 00:01:19.049
She can really write.

00:01:19.049 --> 00:01:20.689
She’s a good writer.

00:01:20.689 --> 00:01:21.819
So let’s meet.”

00:01:21.819 --> 00:01:28.619
We tried to bring that movie to a network
but no one would buy it because it was a little

00:01:28.619 --> 00:01:32.869
too sensual, it was a little to risqué, and
it had to do with magick and that doesn’t

00:01:32.869 --> 00:01:35.679
really work well with network television.

00:01:35.679 --> 00:01:37.229
So that didn’t work.

00:01:37.229 --> 00:01:44.099
But when she came over that February, we say
down and had lunch with her other partner

00:01:44.099 --> 00:01:45.429
Jina [Panebianco].

00:01:45.429 --> 00:01:50.700
And over tunafish sandwiches she told us this
thought that she had of Passionflix and we

00:01:50.700 --> 00:01:52.099
said “Great!

00:01:52.099 --> 00:01:54.100
It’s a great idea.”

00:01:54.100 --> 00:02:02.539
And we literally started the next day on basically
creating the company, the business plan, put

00:02:02.539 --> 00:02:06.799
together a full proposal and think about how
are we going to do all of this.

00:02:06.799 --> 00:02:15.310
But then I spent the next few months raising
money and it took about a year to raise the

00:02:15.310 --> 00:02:21.650
money and then optioned books and made our
first feature last March.

00:02:21.650 --> 00:02:22.650
Long answer!

00:02:22.650 --> 00:02:28.280
Film Courage: That’s interesting, so you
had never really known Joany (and that’s

00:02:28.280 --> 00:02:32.330
her name, right?) previously it was just that
initial email and you just kind of went on

00:02:32.330 --> 00:02:33.629
a gut feeling that “Wow!

00:02:33.629 --> 00:02:36.790
This is someone I want to work with.”

00:02:36.790 --> 00:02:40.819
Tosca Musk: So the answer is yes.

00:02:40.819 --> 00:02:45.750
I didn’t know Joany very well at all except
for the communication we had on the one screenplay

00:02:45.750 --> 00:02:49.209
that she’d written and that screenplay was
good.

00:02:49.209 --> 00:02:56.319
And as a director when you get to work with
a screenwriter and they are open to your comments

00:02:56.319 --> 00:03:01.250
and your notes and they adjust their screenplay
according to how you see it as a filmmaker,

00:03:01.250 --> 00:03:07.080
that collaboration just forms a deep partnership
to begin with.

00:03:07.080 --> 00:03:08.680
So I didn’t know her personally.

00:03:08.680 --> 00:03:15.120
I’d never met her in person until February
but we’d work together by email and phone

00:03:15.120 --> 00:03:17.609
calls for a few months prior to that.

00:03:17.609 --> 00:03:20.310
And so as a filmmaker, I knew her well.

00:03:20.310 --> 00:03:26.069
Film Courage: Okay so then you raised was
it 4.7 million in seed funding?

00:03:26.069 --> 00:03:27.840
Tosca Musk: 4.75.

00:03:27.840 --> 00:03:29.620
Film Courage: 4.75!

00:03:29.620 --> 00:03:30.620
Okay.

00:03:30.620 --> 00:03:31.980
Tosca Musk: 4,753,000.

00:03:31.980 --> 00:03:34.200
Film Courage: Good to know.

00:03:34.200 --> 00:03:36.269
Can you briefly tell us how this happened?

00:03:36.269 --> 00:03:39.530
Did you have specific people in mind you knew
you wanted to approach?

00:03:39.530 --> 00:03:43.889
Tosca Musk: So that was the difficult part.

00:03:43.889 --> 00:03:47.110
Firstly, I’m related to a lot of people
that have raised a lot of people (which is

00:03:47.110 --> 00:03:48.129
helpful).

00:03:48.129 --> 00:03:50.180
And so I went to them for advice.

00:03:50.180 --> 00:03:52.780
What do I do, who do you approach?

00:03:52.780 --> 00:03:54.410
And they basically said “Everybody.”

00:03:54.410 --> 00:03:56.090
You just go to anybody.

00:03:56.090 --> 00:04:00.549
You just constantly tell what the idea is
to every single person that you meet and somebody

00:04:00.549 --> 00:04:05.019
is going to say “Hey, I have somebody who
is going to be interested in that.”

00:04:05.019 --> 00:04:06.019
And that’s what happened.

00:04:06.019 --> 00:04:12.510
I literally just went to every single person
that I knew that had any ability to invest

00:04:12.510 --> 00:04:15.410
and “I said this is the idea, this is what
I’d like to do, do you have any advice for

00:04:15.410 --> 00:04:17.509
me and would you be interested in coming on
board?”

00:04:17.509 --> 00:04:23.020
And some people came on board with $5,000,
some people came on board with $50,000.

00:04:23.020 --> 00:04:28.230
So they weren’t huge amounts, but everybody
that I spoke to wanted to participate because

00:04:28.230 --> 00:04:30.410
they think they idea is really good.

00:04:30.410 --> 00:04:32.470
Film Courage: I’m always wondering how that
happens?

00:04:32.470 --> 00:04:33.740
Is it a long email?

00:04:33.740 --> 00:04:34.740
Is it a phone call?

00:04:34.740 --> 00:04:36.450
Is it when you see them at an event?

00:04:36.450 --> 00:04:38.650
Tosca Musk: It’s all of those things.

00:04:38.650 --> 00:04:43.139
I will take the opportunity to tell people
about Passionflix every single place that

00:04:43.139 --> 00:04:44.139
I go.

00:04:44.139 --> 00:04:47.419
So it will be at a coffeeshop when I’m wearing
a Passionflix t-shirt and I will tell the

00:04:47.419 --> 00:04:48.770
people there.

00:04:48.770 --> 00:04:52.599
It will be at a lunch, it will be at an event.

00:04:52.599 --> 00:04:56.169
I don’t send long emails because most of
the people you are dealing with don’t have

00:04:56.169 --> 00:04:59.080
time to read long emails and they’ll ignore
them.

00:04:59.080 --> 00:05:04.840
So short and to the point with very specific
information in it and what you want.

00:05:04.840 --> 00:05:08.970
What it is that you are looking to do, what
it is that you want and I’m happy to provide

00:05:08.970 --> 00:05:12.729
you with any further supportive documents
for you to review this.

00:05:12.729 --> 00:05:14.099
That was basically what I do.

00:05:14.099 --> 00:05:18.750
I’m about to do it again because we need
to do another raise.

00:05:18.750 --> 00:05:21.960
Film Courage: Is this similar to raising money
for a film?

00:05:21.960 --> 00:05:23.979
Or are they two separate animals?

00:05:23.979 --> 00:05:29.289
Tosca Musk: Raising money for a film, it is
different.

00:05:29.289 --> 00:05:35.580
Because here I’m raising money for a company
that is a distribution company that has an

00:05:35.580 --> 00:05:40.020
overall goal, which is to empower women through
emotional strength while at the same time

00:05:40.020 --> 00:05:42.069
owns multiple movies.

00:05:42.069 --> 00:05:44.979
So we are not making one movie, we are making
50.

00:05:44.979 --> 00:05:52.949
If you invest in Passionflix you get a part
of all 50 movies that we own forever.

00:05:52.949 --> 00:05:57.870
Should the company not do well as a distribution
company, you still have all these assets and

00:05:57.870 --> 00:06:02.409
you’re able to sell them and hopefully we’ll
make that $50,000 back (I’m sure we will).

00:06:02.409 --> 00:06:08.910
That’s why it’s not a difficult ask when
it comes to investment because when you’re

00:06:08.910 --> 00:06:12.970
looking for an investment in one single picture,
it’s basically saying “Hi, I have a movie

00:06:12.970 --> 00:06:13.970
I want to make.

00:06:13.970 --> 00:06:15.560
I’m going to spend 3 million dollars on
this movie.

00:06:15.560 --> 00:06:17.280
Can you give me some money?

00:06:17.280 --> 00:06:20.460
And hopefully everybody else likes this movie
and I can get a distributor and I can get

00:06:20.460 --> 00:06:23.629
it into the theaters or get it into DVD or
some foreign market.

00:06:23.629 --> 00:06:27.090
Hopefully we’ll make our money back and
then you can get your 20%.”

00:06:27.090 --> 00:06:30.419
That’s the individual filmmaking side.

00:06:30.419 --> 00:06:36.060
Which is a different beast and there are a
lot of people that want to invest that way,

00:06:36.060 --> 00:06:40.449
specifically in California or in the U.S.
What I mean is there are tax write-offs that

00:06:40.449 --> 00:06:46.970
are involved, there’s all these different
things that are positive for investors to

00:06:46.970 --> 00:06:50.039
invest in individual films, but that’s not
what we’re looking for.

